        "query_signature": "Choose $x_t$ and observe $Y_t=f_t(x_t)+Z_t$ with $Z_t\\overset{\\mathrm{i.i.d.}}\\sim\\mathcal N(0,\\sigma^2)$. There is one action-point observation per round. Causal policies are allowed and $T,S_{\\mathrm{seg}},k,B,\\sigma$ is public. Switching times and reward functions are hidden. Received feedback may be stored and reused computationally. No unrevealed historical information or extra queries to exhausted samples are available; any within-round full-function or common-sample access must be explicit.",
